{{/*

chezmoi renders this at `chezmoi init` time to generate ~/.config/chezmoi/chezmoi.toml,
which supplies the [data] values that the .tmpl files here depend on. Without it, a
fresh clone fails on its first apply with:

    map has no entry for key "email"

promptStringOnce only prompts when the key is missing from existing config data, so
re-running `chezmoi init` on a configured machine is a no-op, not an interrogation.

To answer non-interactively, pass the *prompt text* as the key (not the variable name):

    chezmoi init --promptString "Email address=you@example.com" \
                 --promptChoice "Is this a work or personal machine=work"

machineType ("personal" or "work") picks Brewfile.personal or Brewfile.work in Brewfile.tmpl.

*/}}
{{- $email := promptStringOnce . "email" "Email address" -}}
{{- $machineType := promptChoiceOnce . "machineType" "Is this a work or personal machine" (list "personal" "work") -}}

[data]
    email = {{ $email | quote }}
    machineType = {{ $machineType | quote }}
